Experiment No.: 3
Title

Demonstration of Arduino Data Types

Aim

To demonstrate different data types used in Arduino programming.

Theory

Arduino supports different data types such as integer, float, character, and boolean. These data types are used to store different types of values in a program.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
USB Cable
Computer/Laptop
Procedure
Connect Arduino Uno to the computer.
Open Arduino IDE.
Declare variables using different data types.
Display the values using Serial Monitor.
Compile and upload the program.
Observe the displayed output.
Code
int number = 100;
float temperature = 36.5;
char grade = 'A';
bool status = true;

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);

  Serial.println(number);
  Serial.println(temperature);
  Serial.println(grade);
  Serial.println(status);
}

void loop()
{
}
Output

Serial Monitor displays:

100
36.5
A
1
Result

Different Arduino data types were successfully demonstrated.

Conclusion

Various Arduino data types were studied and their values were displayed successfully using Serial Monitor.
